  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Given $2 x-y+2 z=2, x-2 y+z=-4$, $x+y+\\lambda z=4$, then the value of $\\lambda$ such that the given system of equation has no solution is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3RSv8",
      "text": "\r\n$-3$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "exMCK",
      "text": "\r\n1\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pL7D9",
      "text": "\r\n0\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IOcDX",
      "text": "\r\n3",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, the system has no solution.\r\n$\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & \\lambda\\end{array}\\right|=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow 2(-2 \\lambda+1)+1(\\lambda+1)+2(3)=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad-4 \\lambda+2+\\lambda+1+6=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 3 \\lambda=9 \\Rightarrow \\lambda=3$",
    "image": null
  },
